  "rhythm": "Twitch owner credit: Acry. Hooktheory public song yvmrJMWvmOW supplies the note-level melody, gaps, C-minor key, 4/4 meter, chord changes and 128 BPM. Adjacent re-attacks of the same pitch are tied into one hold so the quarter-beat ornaments do not slow the entire ocarina performance. This arrangement uses source beats 1-44 (43 beats, 20.16 seconds), ending after the complete G-F-Ab-G fanfare answer rather than cutting its final note. The public MuseScore MLB Theme score is the second notation reference. Melody is untransposed and already fits C4-D5. Trumpet doubles it down an octave; French horn, trombone and bass follow Hooktheory's chord roots and fifths. With no isolated source drum track available, the custom march kit is the repository's permitted fallback, with quiet hats added at otherwise unsupported melody onsets for exact synchronization. Heavier remix for ReiMasa: every notated ocarina gap is removed by sustaining the preceding source pitch to the next onset, so no new melody notes are invented. The band keeps the same Hooktheory chord and melody events but remaps them to OoT synth bass, church organ, trombone and tuba; reinforced kick/snare, open hats, phrase-end tom fills and impact crashes make the percussion substantially heavier. 2023-video retarget for ReiMasa: the requested 101SKC upload is the 54-second current MLB on FOX cue. A March 2024 MuseScore transcription of the same current theme runs 52 seconds and documents six parts: trumpet, French horn, guitar, bass guitar and drum group. The backing is therefore rebuilt around those roles using supported OoT trumpet, horn, nylon-guitar and finger-bass programs, replacing the earlier organ/tuba interpretation. The Hooktheory melody remains the exact written note source; all ocarina gaps stay removed by sustaining the preceding note.",
